\newlabel{fig:ambig_cel_frac_curves}{{3}{7}{Mean performance and mean hyperparameter CV as a function of negative sign percentage for the ambiguous-edge \textit {C.\ elegans} topology with real weights, in which complex or unknown neurotransmitter signs are assigned using fixed counts of 452 negative and 1412 positive edges. The truncated IPC diagnostic is denoted in orange, GR in red, MC in blue, and KR in green. Points show averages across 200 trials for each fraction. The black dot denotes the negative sign percentage of the ambiguous-edge connectome}{figure.3}{}}
